{"id": "EUVD-2026-55454", "enisaUuid": "f0cead04-becd-37a8-bc2f-d866652c8a68", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: ath6kl: fix OOB read from firmware num_msg in TX complete handler\n\nThe firmware-controlled num_msg field (u8, 0-255) drives the loop in\nath6kl_wmi_tx_complete_event_rx() without validation against the buffer\nlength. This allows out-of-bounds reads of up to 1020 bytes past the\nWMI event buffer when the firmware sends an inflated num_msg.\n\nAdd a check that the buffer is large enough to hold the fixed struct\nand the num_msg variable-length entries.", "datePublished": "2026-08-10T12:03:30", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T21:09:06", "baseScore": 8.1, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:A/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5297299c3fa6133275db0be99d69cd759b6cbfe9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/35196a07603f8c94a4943093bc26d5b5826285f8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0e0fc04af9b443c6b425f00fb604ff599bc80d1d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/69ac7ba3a3df6654e7daa82674575a8c4a1a63ea", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/289edc3c71344b89e6522891147cfb8f61b088bb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/eb636fbc443149b3501c3f97e26225ddcb314a0f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c38b0d5c661951b5dd082bdf31f8a57a0ce6e540", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3a21c89215cc18f1a97c5e5bfd1da6d4f3d44495"], "aliases": ["GHSA-2244-8pcv-8jr6", "CVE-2026-68353"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.29, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0a90d07d-e270-3e2c-9169-332c7501db32", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3.2"}, {"id": "22880baa-d66f-3497-ac3d-1ab58b89d944", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.216"}, {"id": "2d25e6d0-410d-3ccf-b6e2-b50b86b97e53", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.265"}, {"id": "2d63b3fb-99a5-3